before:
With max-content, the label uses its unwrapped text width, exceeding this 100px container.
```css
.demo { writing-mode: horizontal-tb; direction: ltr; }
.wrap { width: 100px; } .label { font: 16px/20px monospace; width: max-content; }
```

after:
The label says “one two three” inside a 100-pixel wrapper.

```css
.wrap {
  width: 100px;
}
.label {
  font: 16px/20px monospace;
  width: fit-content;
}
```

`fit-content` uses the available space while staying between the content’s minimum and maximum widths.
